\b\fs36\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2914973\charrsid2914973 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc232416652}3.1 Password Security and Hashing{\*\bkmkend _Toc232416652}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2914973 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs32\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2914973\charrsid2914973 The application enforces strict data protection guidelines regarding user credentials. Under no circumstances are plain-text passwords stored in the database. Instead, the system relies on a s
ecure, industry-standard cryptographic hashing algorithm:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\sa160\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2914973 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2914973\charrsid2914973 
Algorithm: The backend utilizes the PASSWORD_BCRYPT algorithm via PHP's native password_hash() function.
\par Salting: A unique, secure, and random salt is automatically generated by the algorithm for every password before hashing. This mitigates the risk of rainbow table attacks.
\par Verification: During authentication (login_process.php), the user-submitted password is verified against the stored hash using password_verify(). This function executes in constant time, preventing timing attacks aimed at guessing valid password hashes.

\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s26\ql \li0\ri0\sa60\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2914973 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\fs36\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2914973\charrsid2914973 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc232416653}3.2 Access Control and Page Protection{\*\bkmkend _Toc232416653}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2914973 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs32\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2914973\charrsid2914973 The system implements Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) to separate regular customers from administrative users.
\par Session Isolation: Access states are managed completely on the server-side via PHP $_SESSION. When a user authenticates, their database identifier (user_id) and assigned privilege level (role) are bound to their session token.
\par Admin Panel Guarding: To protect administrative entry points like admin.php and processing scripts like auth/add_product.php, strict validation gates are embedded at the very top of the execution flow:
\par 
\par PHP
\par if (!isset($_SESSION['user_id']) || !isset($_SESSION['role']) || $_SESSION['role'] !== 'admin') \{
\par     die("Access denied. You are not an admin.");
\par \}
\par If an unauthenticated user or a standard customer attempts to access this resource directly via URL manipulation, the script terminates execution immediately before rendering any interface components or database content.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s26\ql \li0\ri0\sa60\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2914973 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\fs36\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2914973\charrsid2914973 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc232416654}3.3 Database Security and Query Safety{\*\bkmkend _Toc232416654}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2914973 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs32\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2914973\charrsid2914973 To safeguard the system against one of the most critical web vulnerabilities\emdash SQL Injection (SQLi)\emdash 
the database interaction layer avoids dynamic string concatenation for user-supplied variables:
\par Prepared Statements: All dynamic interactions (such as updating order statuses in admin.php or submitting registration forms) utilize parameterized prepared statements through the MySQLi extension.
\par Separation of Code and Data: By binding parameters separately ($stmt->bind_param("si", $new_status, $order_id)), 
the database engine treats user inputs strictly as literal values rather than executable SQL commands, neutralizing potential exploit payloads.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s26\ql \li0\ri0\sa60\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2914973 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\fs36\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2914973\charrsid2914973 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc232416655}3.4 Data Sanitization and Output Encoding{\*\bkmkend _Toc232416655}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2914973 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs32\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2914973\charrsid2914973 To protect administrators and clients from Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)
 injections within interactive tables and dashboards (e.g., viewing customer names and addresses in the order log), data is processed before rendering:
\par 
\par Context-Aware Encoding: Customer data retrieved from the database is processed through the htmlspecialchars() function with the ENT_QUOTES and UTF-8 flags active.
\par This structure guarantees that malicious HTML tags or malicious JavaScript blocks (<script>) submitted inside user profiles or checkout forms are safely converted into harmless text literals when rendered in the Admin Panel interface.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid12349098 \tab }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid12349098\charrsid12349098 
