\b\fs48\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning32\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10517967 \page }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid3763249\charrsid3763249 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc232416656}Technologies Used}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid3609045 {\*\bkmkend _Toc232416656}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2914973 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs32\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2914973\charrsid2914973 
PHP: The core server-side language of the project. I chose it because it is the industry standard for dynamic web development, offers native database integration, and allows for rapid prototyping of e-commerce business logic.
\par MySQL: The relational database management system used to store structured data. It handles critical application states, including user credentials, product catalogs, variant configurations (size, color, stock), and itemized customer orders through stric
tly normalized tables.
\par MySQLi (PHP Extension): A core native driver used to establish secure communication between the PHP backend and the MySQL database. It provides support for prepared statements, which completely isolate execution paths from user-supp
lied inputs to eliminate SQL injection risks.
\par HTML5 & CSS3: Used to build the user interface presentation layer. Crafted from scratch, the design implements a modern, minimalist grid layout for the product showcase, interactive forms, and a responsive adm
in dashboard equipped with dynamic, status-colored visual indicators.
\par JavaScript (Vanilla JS): The client-side scripting language used to enhance interactivity. It manages global state tokens (such as user session parameters), coordinates shopping cart up
dates, and handles user interface actions like dynamically toggling detailed order logs.
\par Git & GitHub: Used for version control to track code changes linearly, manage production-ready branches, and ensure the entire repository is safely backed up, structured, and documented.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2914973 
